-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NASA / PDS DATA PROVENANCE
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEEPSIFT reads public Mars Science Laboratory (Curiosity) archives from the NASA Planetary Data System:

* REMS (Rover Environmental Monitoring Station) — MSL-M-REMS-5-MODRDR-V1.0, PDS Atmospheres Node.
  The REMS instrument was provided by Spain's Centro de Astrobiología (CAB).
* RAD (Radiation Assessment Detector) — MSL-M-RAD-3-RDR-V1.0, PDS Planetary Plasma Interactions (PPI) Node.
  Data produced by the MSL RAD team (Southwest Research Institute and partners).
* Navcam (Navigation Cameras) raw EDR — MSLNAV_0XXX, PDS Imaging Node / JPL
  (https://planetarydata.jpl.nasa.gov/img/data/msl/MSLNAV_0XXX/).
* PLACES rover localizations (localized_interp.csv) — PDS Imaging Node
  (https://planetarydata.jpl.nasa.gov/img/data/msl/msl_places/).

The repository does NOT redistribute the Navcam imagery or PLACES tables. It commits only DEEPSIFT-generated manifests
(data/manifests/*.json) that record each product's public PDS URL, label metadata and SHA-256, so users download the
source data themselves (scripts/fetch_navcam.py, scripts/fetch_nasa.py).

Bundled offline sample: data/fixtures/msl_curiosity/ contains gzip-compressed, unmodified copies of 24 public REMS and RAD
PDS products (sols 238–243, ≈4.6 MB) used as the LOCAL_NASA_SAMPLE offline fallback and in tests. They are public
NASA/PDS source data, not owned by DEEPSIFT and not covered by the Apache License; each file's original PDS URL and
SHA-256 are listed in data/fixtures/msl_curiosity/MANIFEST.json.

